<Item XName="Page" Type="PageMgr" />
<Item XName="Read_me" UserName="Read_me" Type="Notes">
<Selected><T>Bool</T><D>0</D></Selected>
<Text>&lt;P class=MsoTitle style=&quot;BORDER-TOP: medium none; BORDER-RIGHT: medium none; BORDER-BOTTOM: windowtext 0.75pt solid; PADDING-BOTTOM: 1pt; PADDING-TOP: 0in; PADDING-LEFT: 0in; BORDER-LEFT: medium none; MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; PADDING-RIGHT: 0in&quot; align=center&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;&lt;FONT size=5 face=Arial&gt;Radar Spectrasys&amp;nbsp;RFLink&amp;nbsp;Phased Array Simulation Example&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;TEXT-ALIGN: center; MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot; align=center&gt;&lt;EM&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: Arial; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt&quot;&gt;Keysight Technologies SystemVue Example&amp;nbsp;Workspace&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;?xml:namespace prefix = &quot;o&quot; ns = &quot;urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:office&quot; /&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/EM&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;TEXT-ALIGN: center; MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot; align=center&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;FONT size=2&gt;&lt;FONT size=2&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&lt;FONT size=2&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;&lt;BR&gt;&lt;FONT size=2&gt;This example proposes radar system simulation with&amp;nbsp;Spectrasys&amp;nbsp;PhasedArray RFLink based&amp;nbsp;designs. The traditional 3-layer architecure is applied with one target and one monostatic radar. From the perspective of RF phased array modeling method, one Basic design (using Spectrasys built-in RF phased array parts) and one advanced (using Spectrasys RF phased array parts + ADI ADAR1000 chipset parametric designs) are proposed. For this workspace, the 8*8 for both Tx and Rx phased array designs are presented.&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;&lt;FONT size=2&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;&lt;FONT size=2&gt;For both design methods, phased array pointing angle defined beam weights are calculated by the BeamformerWeights parts and transferred to the Spectrasys&amp;nbsp;RF_Link phased array&amp;nbsp;channels. Then the Tx envelop signal is transported to the Air Interface parts (inside magenta blocks) to regroup the signal from Tx channel sizing to target number sizing. After the virtual PhasedArrayTx, EchoGenerator and PhasedArrayRx, the signal sizing is transformed back to Rx channel number and the Rx beamforming is performed.&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;&lt;FONT size=2&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;&lt;FONT size=2&gt;The Tx waveformed is designed as simplified LFM, and signal processing chain is realized by pulse compression and PD. The range-doppler matrix and PD result are presented. The filtering incurred delay compensations (Const + ChopVarOffset after pulse compression part) are bypassed, since without filters in dataflow design no additional delays are involved.&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;&lt;FONT size=2&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;&lt;FONT size=2&gt;The SystemLevel_Parameters equation provides all system level parameters, including phased array design parameters. After all simulations are done, the Equation_ResultPlots_Basic or _Advanced&amp;nbsp;equation helps the user to plot the RD map and PD result figures.&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;FONT color=#ff0000 size=2&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;Folders in this workspace:&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;UL&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;LI&gt;&lt;FONT face=Arial&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;1.&amp;nbsp;Result_Figures_Advanced&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/LI&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;UL&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;LI&gt;&lt;FONT face=Arial&gt;Contains&amp;nbsp;RD Matrix and PD result for Advanced&amp;nbsp;phased array design simulation using ADAR1000&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;FONT face=Arial&gt;&amp;nbsp;beamforming chipset parameters.&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/LI&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;LI&gt;&lt;FONT face=Arial&gt;These figures are obtained by enabling the &quot;bigger&quot; phased array RF_Link part in the RadarSys_Main schematic in SystemDesign_PhasedArray_RFLink folder.&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/LI&gt;&lt;/UL&gt;&lt;FONT face=Arial&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;LI&gt;&lt;FONT face=Arial&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;2.&amp;nbsp;Result_Figures_Basic&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/LI&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;UL&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;LI&gt;&lt;FONT face=Arial&gt;Contains&amp;nbsp;RD Matrix and PD result for&amp;nbsp;basic&amp;nbsp;phased array design simulation using built-in Spectrasys RF beamforming parts.&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/LI&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;LI&gt;&lt;FONT face=Arial&gt;These figures are obtained by enabling the &quot;smaller&quot; phased array RF_Link part in the RadarSys_Main schematic in SystemDesign_PhasedArray_RFLink folder.&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/LI&gt;&lt;/UL&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;LI&gt;&lt;FONT face=Arial&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;3. Result_Figures_RFImpairmentCompare&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/LI&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;UL&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;LI&gt;&lt;FONT face=Arial&gt;Contains complex signal behavior comparisons between no impairment case and with impairment case for the Basic mode simulation (see above topic-2 for confiiguration).&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/LI&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;LI&gt;&lt;FONT face=Arial&gt;User can check the signal distortions at various positions of the phased array design due to RF impairment effects.&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/LI&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;LI&gt;&lt;FONT face=Arial&gt;For demonstration purposes, two major RF impairments are considered: phased array multi-channel amplitude error and phase error.&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/LI&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;UL&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;LI&gt;&lt;FONT face=Arial&gt;For amplitude error, Normal error distribution with 1dB stddev is applied for both Tx and Rx array attenuators;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/LI&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;LI&gt;&lt;FONT face=Arial&gt;For phase error, Normal error distribution with 5deg stddev is applied for both Tx and Rx array phase shifters;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/LI&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;LI&gt;&lt;FONT face=Arial&gt;For the RF phased array configurations in this workspace, the Tx RF impairment incurred RF&amp;nbsp;distortions is more severe than the Rx side.&amp;nbsp; &lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/LI&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;LI&gt;&lt;FONT face=Arial&gt;The &quot;NoImpair&quot; dataset can be generated by selecting &quot;None&quot; for error type of amplitude and phase components in Main1/2 schematics, respectively.&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/LI&gt;&lt;/UL&gt;&lt;/UL&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;LI&gt;&lt;FONT face=Arial&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;4. Spectrasys_PhasedArray_Advanced&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/LI&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;UL&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;LI&gt;&lt;FONT face=Arial&gt;This folder includes the detailed modeling by ADAR1000 both for Tx array and Rx array.&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/LI&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;LI&gt;&lt;FONT face=Arial&gt;For Rx/Tx design, user is required to run the PhArrayDesign_Params first, then go to RunSim equation for array configuration and pattern plots.&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/LI&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;LI&gt;&lt;FONT face=Arial&gt;The &quot;Chipset_Modeling&quot; folder contains parametric chipset design mapping to SystemVue models/subnets.&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/LI&gt;&lt;/UL&gt;&lt;FONT face=Arial&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;LI&gt;&lt;FONT face=Arial&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;5. Spectrasys_PhasedArray_Basic&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/LI&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;UL&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;LI&gt;&lt;FONT face=Arial&gt;This folder includes the detailed modeling by&amp;nbsp;built-in Spectrasys&amp;nbsp;phased array parts&amp;nbsp;both for Tx array and Rx array.&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/LI&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;LI&gt;&lt;FONT face=Arial&gt;For Rx/Tx design, user is required to run the PhasedArray1/2 analysis first, then go to&amp;nbsp;PlotPattern_Tx/Rx for&amp;nbsp;pattern plots.&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/LI&gt;&lt;/UL&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;FONT face=Arial&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;LI&gt;&lt;FONT face=Arial&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;6. SystemDesign_PhasedArray_RFLink&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/LI&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;UL&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;LI&gt;&lt;FONT face=Arial&gt;The Coupling 8*8 case folder defines an optional Tx element-to-element coupling design.&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/LI&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;LI&gt;&lt;FONT face=Arial&gt;The high level radar system simulation is realized in &quot;RadarSys_Main&quot; schematic. User can select &quot;Basic&quot; or &quot;Advanced&quot;&amp;nbsp;phased array modeling method by enabling the &quot;smaller&quot; or &quot;bigger&quot; phased array RFLink parts, both for Tx and Rx.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/LI&gt;&lt;/UL&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/UL&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;</Text>
